# Integer128 power promotes mixed operands

Verifies every narrower signed integer width participates in int128 power in
both operand orders and produces an int128 result.

>>> source
narrow8: int8 = 2
narrow16: int16 = 2
narrow32: int32 = 2
narrow64: int64 = 2
wide: int128 = 3

result8_base: int128 = narrow8 ** wide
result8_exponent: int128 = wide ** narrow8
result16_base: int128 = narrow16 ** wide
result16_exponent: int128 = wide ** narrow16
result32_base: int128 = narrow32 ** wide
result32_exponent: int128 = wide ** narrow32
result64_base: int128 = narrow64 ** wide
result64_exponent: int128 = wide ** narrow64
print(result8_base)
print(result8_exponent)
print(result16_base)
print(result16_exponent)
print(result32_base)
print(result32_exponent)
print(result64_base)
print(result64_exponent)

<<< stdout
8
9
8
9
8
9
8
9

<<< stderr
